# ForPost whitelist configuration
# Each line is a command prefix that is allowed in whitelist mode.
# Empty lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# The command must START WITH one of these prefixes to be allowed.
#
# whitelist runs as the unprivileged RESTRICTED_COMMAND_USER (no docker group),
# so ONLY read commands belong here. It is the "read the work repo" mode: pure
# GitHub-API reads via gh, plus local repo inspection. Deliberately NO writes,
# NO local-clone mutation (git pull/fetch), and NO docker (those are full-access)
# - so ForPost can never push to or mutate the work environment from here.

# gh read-only (view PRs / repos / issues / their comments).
# Write actions (gh repo create, gh pr merge/create/comment, ...) are full-access.
gh pr list
gh pr view
gh pr diff
gh pr status
gh pr checks
gh issue list
gh issue view
gh repo view

# local repo inspection (read-only; operate on an already-present clone).
git status
git log
